From d5aa9934975d4573b1b4235d7bf34f556f0d3936 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:11:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: the subtitle search after a seek also after a
 subtitle change read again

A change of an embedded subtitle stream of a file no longer seeks the
player: the demuxer alone goes back to the time on screen and the
packets it reads again for audio and video are dropped (Piers,
"[VideoPlayer] Do not interrupt playback on embedded subtitle change").
Before, that seek flushed the buffers, and FlushBuffers() started the
search of Hades for the text lines on screen at the target that are
stored before where the demuxer reads again (SubtitleSeekSearch.h): in
Matroska the demuxer goes back to the cluster of the video keyframe, so
a line that started before that cluster is never read again, and stayed
off screen until the next line. Without the seek that search was no
longer started: a subtitle stream chosen during playback showed nothing
until its next line.

The re-read starts the same search, with the target a seek to the same
time would give it (the demuxer time in DVD_TIME_BASE, less the subtitle
delay). The search waits for the clock to pass the target as it does
after a seek, which it already has, and what it finds goes to the
subtitle player as after a seek, decoded once whether the search or the
demuxer gives it first (CSubtitleSeekSeen). Where the player seeks
instead (another input, fast-forward or rewind, a time offset), nothing
changes: FlushBuffers() starts it as before.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
index 12e86cf..77de6ab 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -5250,6 +5250,12 @@ bool CVideoPlayer::RereadSubtitleData()
   m_CurrentAudio.replaying = m_CurrentAudio.id >= 0;
   m_CurrentVideo.replaying = m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0;
 
+  // Hades: the text lines on screen now that are stored before where the demuxer reads again, as
+  // after a seek (SubtitleSeekSearch.h): FlushBuffers() starts that search, and a re-read has none.
+  // The target is the one a seek to this time would give it.
+  StartSubtitleSearch(DVD_MSEC_TO_TIME(static_cast<double>(time.count())) -
+                      m_VideoPlayerVideo->GetSubtitleDelay());
+
   CLog::LogF(LOGDEBUG, "re-reading subtitle data from demuxer time {}", time.count());
   return true;
 }
